        "chars_per_1k_ink": 6000.0
      }
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        200,
        402,
        1075,
        581
      ],
      "category": "Text",
      "text": "(b) If the time urgency of the emergency is such as to preclude development of a formal contract, the Agency may use a Letter of Intent informing the contractor of: (1) the scope of the work to be done, (2) the cost and time limitations, and (3) the fact that the Letter of Intent is subject to later confirmation in the form of a formal contract. Copies of the Letter of Intent shall be sent forthwith to the Comptroller, the Director of the Budget and the Corporation Counsel.",
      "logprob_stats": {
        "bbox": {
          "n_tokens": 19,
          "mean": -0.1708,
          "min": -1.1888
        },
        "category": {
          "n_tokens": 1,
